97
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:30,080
No, he was most likely
just an ordinary young man.

98
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:33,259
He joined the mafia sometime later,

99
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:36,357
which means something
from his previous life

100
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:39,520
will tell us who the boss
really was 15 years ago.

101
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:44,637
And you are the best person to
find that something. Think back.

102
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:45,920
Anything can help.

103
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:48,477
Can you think of any
stories from your childhood?

104
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:50,913
Maybe some your mother used to tell you?

105
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,680
Kill di Volpe. There.

106
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,500
Kill di Volpe?

107
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:58,500
The Bay of the Fox?

108
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,110
That's right.

109
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:02,917
It's a rather famous resort
on the costa Smeralda.

110
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,941
She said that's how the two of them
met, while she was on vacation.

111
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:10,959
She also told me that my
father grew up in Sardinia.

112
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:14,046
Apparently, he spoke
with a Sardinian dialect.

113
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:16,546
Then he just up and vanished.

114
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:20,586
Mom never found out anything else
about him, not even his name.

115
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:22,877
That's everything I know.

116
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:24,640
Beyond that, I'm at a loss.

117
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:29,020
And besides, it's just
my mom's reminiscing.

118
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:33,180
You are the only living
relative the boss has left.

119
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:37,892
You threaten his precious anonymity,
which is why he's fighting to end you.

120
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,740
Squalo di Volpe, huh?

121
